# RapidRecall

RapidRecall is an Android memory game developed for CMPUT 301 using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.

The user selects a sequence length from 1 to 10 digits. The application displays the randomly generated digits one at a time, after which the user attempts to reproduce the sequence. Each completed attempt is logged and contributes to the session summary.

## Features

- Selectable sequence length from 1–10 digits
- Timed digit-by-digit sequence presentation
- User sequence input and correctness feedback
- Attempt logging
- Session statistics including:
  - Total attempts
  - Successful attempts
  - Failed attempts
  - Overall accuracy
- Attempt log containing:
  - Attempt number
  - Sequence length
  - Target sequence
  - User input
  - Success/failure
  - Timestamp

## AI Use Disclosure

OpenAI ChatGPT was used during the development of this assignment.

AI assistance was used extensively as a development and learning aid, including:

- Reviewing the assignment requirements and permitted AI-use policy
- Discussing and refining the object-oriented architecture
- Reviewing the responsibilities and relationships of `Sequence`, `Attempt`, `Round`, and `GameSession`
- Explaining Kotlin and Jetpack Compose concepts such as:
  - `val` versus `var`
  - Compose state and recomposition
  - `mutableStateOf`
  - `remember`
  - `LaunchedEffect`
  - Composable screen organization
- Generating portions of Kotlin/Jetpack Compose code used in the application
- Assisting with UI organization and styling
- Assisting with debugging and refactoring as the object model changed

AI-generated code incorporated into the submitted project is identified with comments in the relevant source files.

The developer reviewed, modified, tested, and takes responsibility for all submitted code and documentation.

